WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.700
- So you've also re-released
your Christmas album.

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.220
Hard Candy Christmas is a classic.

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:07.290
It is hard to have a
classic at Christmas too.

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:08.250
Like, you know what I'm saying?

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:10.230
Like we all go to the White
Christmas, the Holy Nights,

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:11.700
the Silent that kind of thing.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:15.660
But that song, one, I just
had a question because is it,

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.100
have you always been able to write

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.450
with that kind of vulnerability?

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:21.270
- Well actually I did not
write Hard Candy Christmas.

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:24.420
Everybody thinks I did. The
girl that wrote all of that,

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.730
the music from The Best Little Whorehouse

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:28.200
in Texas wrote that.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.033
- Cause that's where it's from.

00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:30.270
- It's from The Best Little Whorehouse.

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:33.300
But I love that song and
people always tag it to me.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.260
But I get a lot of credit

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.210
for a lot of stuff a lot of people do

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.370
just because I'm singing it or because...

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:39.840
- Well, no, because
you write a bunch of...

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:40.771
- I do.

00:00:40.771 --> 00:00:41.604
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:41.604 --> 00:00:42.437
- That's one of the ones I did not write

00:00:42.437 --> 00:00:44.970
but everybody thinks I
did and I wish I had.

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:46.590
- I know. But here's the thing though

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:49.110
about that is that's the
storyteller in you too though.

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.090
Like it's very, cause
that's what I'm saying.

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:52.500
Like everybody thought that was you

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.240
because how you tell that story

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:57.240
is I mean, it just breaks your heart

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:59.280
in the most amazing way.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.470
But it also, I think you being vulnerable

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:03.131
with even with a Coat of Many Colors,

00:01:03.131 --> 00:01:05.130
all the songs, literally any song,

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:08.280
like you were a fantastic
writer, not just singer

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.140
which is amazing, but it opens up

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:12.270
so many doors for us to be, you know,

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:14.430
as a little kid, I didn't
think any differently.

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:15.750
I thought a woman could speak her mind.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:17.940
I thought a woman could
say how she was feeling

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:18.773
and that was okay.

00:01:18.773 --> 00:01:19.800
I thought that, and I know my mom

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:22.800
and her generation couldn't.
They didn't have that luxury.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:24.240
So it's just a thank you really.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:25.584
- Oh, you've made up for it.

00:01:25.584 --> 00:01:26.417
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:26.417 --> 00:01:27.968
- I did.

00:01:27.968 --> 00:01:29.667
- You can say what you want any time.

00:01:29.667 --> 00:01:31.703
- Oh, you should hear my next album.

00:01:31.703 --> 00:01:33.120
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:34.620
I made up for it.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:37.080
- It is snowing in Tahoe.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:38.370
- Oh, it must be beautiful.

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:39.750
- And it's making me homesick

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:41.760
for how snow's back home at Christmas.

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:44.070
So magical and peaceful.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:47.610
But Sam, it is only mid-October

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:50.610
and I'm thinking that
is some kind of a sign.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:53.070
- Maybe some of that magic dust
you're always talking about.

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:56.142
- Well, honestly, I do think
it's more than a coincidence.

00:01:56.142 --> 00:01:58.290
I think it's a sign
that I should bring some

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:01.710
of that mountain magic to
everybody this Christmas.

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:04.773
Why don't we do a special from Dollywood?

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:06.743
- Welcome back y'all.

00:02:06.743 --> 00:02:09.926
We've got the incomparable
Dolly Parton with us on now.

00:02:09.926 --> 00:02:11.117
(crowd applauding and cheering)

00:02:11.117 --> 00:02:12.840
- That was another look at her new movie,

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:14.670
Dolly Parton's Mountain Magic Christmas.

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:16.920
It premiers today on NBC.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:20.310
So by the way, I love that
it's called Mountain Magics.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:21.600
Why did you call it that?

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:24.330
- Well, because to me
the mountains are magic,

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:26.670
especially the Smokey Mountains
where I was born and raised,

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:29.160
all that beautiful. I mean
it's so beautiful out there.

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.080
And of course everybody
should always be proud

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.670
of their home wherever you're from.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:33.503
- Yeah.

00:02:33.503 --> 00:02:34.710
- But there's always the magic

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:36.930
in the mountains for
me because that's home.

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:38.070
That's where mom and daddy were.

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:40.410
That's where I grew up with
my brothers and sisters.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:41.970
That's where all my memories, you know,

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:44.640
started and growing up in
that little country church,

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:45.900
my grandpa was a preacher.

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:49.410
So it's magic to me when I
get a chance to go home now.

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:51.210
And so I always keep that

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:53.070
with me and I think that's important

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:54.690
and that's kind of what the show is about,

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:56.730
trying to capture that magic again.

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:58.170
- Yeah I love that.

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:01.260
Okay, so you also just released
a greatest hits collection

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:02.850
called Diamonds and Rhinestones.

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:03.704
I love the title.

00:03:03.704 --> 00:03:04.537
(Dolly laughing)

00:03:04.537 --> 00:03:05.640
- Is it true that your song Two Doors Down

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:06.930
was about fried clams?

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:08.340
- It was. But see...

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:09.660
- I need this story.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:10.493
- I'm like you.

00:03:10.493 --> 00:03:13.650
No, I've always had
problem with my weight too.

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:14.483
- Oh, up and down.

00:03:14.483 --> 00:03:15.510
- I love to eat. I've been up and down.

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:16.950
I've been every size in the world.

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:20.250
And a long time ago, it
was getting me depressed.

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:21.780
I didn't like it. So I was, you know,

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:24.510
you try everything to lose weight.

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:27.660
And I had got on some
kind of crazy old diet,

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:29.190
like a liquid protein.

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:30.750
You just drink an ounce of something

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:33.109
that's ground up horse hooves
or something. I don't know.

00:03:33.109 --> 00:03:34.287
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:34.287 --> 00:03:36.657
- I don't know or monkey pee or something.

00:03:36.657 --> 00:03:38.223
I don't know what it
was, but it was just...

00:03:38.223 --> 00:03:39.632
- This will make you slimmer.

00:03:39.632 --> 00:03:41.820
- Yeah, but you supposed to drink it

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:44.250
like three times a day
and it was so ungodly.

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:45.170
You just have to close the back

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:47.100
of your throat off so you don't smell.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:48.600
You know how it goes but.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:49.433
- No thanks.

00:03:49.433 --> 00:03:53.310
- We used to stay at the
Howard Johnson's Motor Lodge,

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:55.410
the band when we traveled
back in the early days

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:56.790
and they had a restaurant there

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:58.770
and they had these fried clams

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:02.160
that we couldn't wait to stop
to go to Howard Johnson's.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:03.360
Even if we weren't staying over,

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:05.910
we'd stop to eat the fried clams.

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:07.200
But we were staying over and I was

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:11.640
on that stupid liquid protein
diet and the band was down

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:14.400
in the kitchen and I was
in a hallway in my room

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.830
and I could hear them
all laughing and talking.

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:17.790
- That's I'm saying you.
You start to lose time.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:18.690
- And I would start singing.

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:22.224
I was just saying like two doors down.

00:04:22.224 --> 00:04:24.386
♪ Two doors down, they're
laughing and drinking ♪

00:04:24.386 --> 00:04:25.888
♪ And having a party ♪

00:04:25.888 --> 00:04:29.770
♪ But two doors down, they're
not a aware that I'm around ♪

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:33.510
♪ But here I am just crying
my heart out feeling sorry ♪

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:34.465
- Over fried clams.

00:04:34.465 --> 00:04:37.620
♪ Having a party just two doors down ♪

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:39.330
- I was just in there
feeling sorry for myself

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:41.850
cause they was eating
fried clams and I wasn't.

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:42.683
(audience laughing)

00:04:42.683 --> 00:04:44.640
- I love that that song is about that.

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:45.473
- And it was two doors down.

00:04:45.473 --> 00:04:48.390
I was staying two doors
down from the restaurant.

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:50.730
That's why I... seriously.

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:52.770
- But one of your biggest hits

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:55.350
was I Will Always Love
You. You did write that.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:58.650
Do you remember the first time
you heard Whitney's version?

00:04:58.650 --> 00:04:59.550
- Yes.

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:01.890
- Cause I grew up hearing yours

00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:03.540
and then all of a sudden
The Bodyguard happened.

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:05.070
I'm just curious, what was your first,

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:05.903
cause it's your baby?

00:05:05.903 --> 00:05:07.230
- Well, there's a little story about that.

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:10.080
When they were doing The Bodyguard movie,

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:12.330
they had chosen another
song for the theme song

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:15.360
and someone came out with that very song

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:17.070
right when they were about
to put the movie out.

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:19.080
And they were, they were drastic to.

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:22.290
I mean they were really
trying to find a great song

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:25.957
and Kevin Costner and
his secretary, they said,

00:05:25.957 --> 00:05:27.570
"Do you remember Dolly Parton's song

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:29.340
of I Will Always Love
You? It's a country song

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:30.420
but it's a beautiful song."

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:32.580
And so they called me to see

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:34.650
if they could use it and I said yes.

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:36.660
And I didn't hear anything else about it.

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:37.980
I didn't know if they had it.

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:39.990
I didn't know if they had done it.

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:44.990
And I was driving my car from
downtown where my office was

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:48.390
on 16th Avenue back to my
house over in Brentwood.

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:50.100
And I was just driving along

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:52.957
and I had the radio on
and I just heard this,

00:05:52.957 --> 00:05:56.550
"If I should stay," you know...

00:05:56.550 --> 00:05:57.550
- Yeah.

00:05:57.550 --> 00:05:58.383
- And it's, you know, it's
one of those things like,

00:05:58.383 --> 00:05:59.880
it's like a dog hearing a whistle.

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:02.460
You know. I go, what is that?

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:03.450
And all of a sudden...

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:04.380
- That's the first?

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:06.630
- And that's the first time.
They hadn't sent it to me.

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:07.463
They did nothing.

00:06:07.463 --> 00:06:08.790
I heard it on the radio.

00:06:08.790 --> 00:06:10.941
And so when it went into...

00:06:10.941 --> 00:06:11.880
♪ And I ♪

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:12.713
- Yeah.

00:06:12.713 --> 00:06:14.370
- And it's like I just freaked out.

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:16.140
I had to pull over to the side

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:18.570
because I honestly
thought I was gonna wreck.

00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:20.880
It was the most overwhelming feeling.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:22.673
And you know how great that was.

00:06:22.673 --> 00:06:23.506
- Oh my god

00:06:23.506 --> 00:06:24.339
- And it was great.

00:06:24.339 --> 00:06:25.980
But that's the story of that.

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:28.860
But when you sang that,
when we did the Academy

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:30.630
of Country Music Awards, when you did that

00:06:30.630 --> 00:06:34.320
at the end, I mean, to
tell you that whole crowd,

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:37.050
Whitney, she would've been so proud of you

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:39.177
cause I felt like she was watching you.

00:06:39.177 --> 00:06:41.700
You absolutely killed it.

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:43.350
Seriously. It was incredible.

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:45.360
And I was so emotional.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:47.340
- Me too right now. Like, I'm just,

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.470
it hit me that you're like
talking about me singing.

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:51.030
It's fine.

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:52.230
- It was great though.

00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:53.063
- No. I will cry.

00:06:53.063 --> 00:06:53.896
- It was incredible.

00:06:53.896 --> 00:06:54.780
- We're not. They're saying
can you do a little&gt;?

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:56.325
No. I will cry. No.

00:06:56.325 --> 00:07:00.439
(audience applauding and cheering)

00:07:00.439 --> 00:07:02.106
- How about,

00:07:02.106 --> 00:07:03.990
how about if I sing a little bit of it

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:05.351
and you sing harmony with me?

00:07:05.351 --> 00:07:06.184
- Okay. Okay.

00:07:06.184 --> 00:07:08.193
- Okay. I'll sing a little bit.

00:07:08.193 --> 00:07:11.629
♪ And I ♪

00:07:11.629 --> 00:07:16.629
♪ Will always love you ♪

00:07:17.639 --> 00:07:22.639
♪ I will always love you ♪

00:07:24.773 --> 00:07:26.335
♪ You ♪

00:07:26.335 --> 00:07:30.002
(audience applauding)

00:07:30.002 --> 00:07:32.623
- It's the little things.

00:07:32.623 --> 00:07:34.239
It's the little things.

00:07:34.239 --> 00:07:36.020
I don't know if y'all heard.

00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:37.830
It was like on will but there's this,

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:40.590
your breaks in your voice are so magical.

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:42.180
You're like a magical fairy human.

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:43.013
I don't know.

00:07:43.013 --> 00:07:44.760
Anyway, so we need another short break.

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:47.100
Dolly's got two collections
of music out now.

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:49.920
A Holly Dolly Christmas
Ultimate Deluxe Edition

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:52.870
and Diamonds and Rhinestones,
the Greatest Hits Collection.

